   "daf": "65b",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "שִׁיסַּע וְלֹא הִבְדִּיל. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְשִׁסַּע״ – אֵין שִׁיסַּע אֶלָּא בַּיָּד, וְכֵן הוּא אוֹמֵר: ״וַיְשַׁסְּעֵהוּ כְּשַׁסַּע הַגְּדִי״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that after removing the crop and the feathers and innards that emerged with it, the priest «ripped» the bird lengthwise «and did not separate» the two halves of the bird. In this regard «the Sages taught» in a baraita: The verse states: «“And he shall rend”» (Leviticus 1:17). The act of «rending is» performed «only by hand, and so too,» the verse «states» with regard to Samson: «“And he rent it as one would have rent a kid,» and he had nothing in his hand” (Judges 14:6)."
  }
 ],
